 "panels": [
  {
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "IP Reputation",
   "description": "What the reputation list is doing, worked out by ip-reputation itself. NO FIREWALL RULE is the one to act on: the list is loaded on the router, but no enabled raw/filter rule references it, so it blocks nothing -- add the two rules from the panel below. LOADING means the router has fewer entries than the merged feeds (a first load is one REST call per entry). NOT CONFIGURED is mikrotik.* missing from suricata.properties. With several routers: the worst router decides the state, Entries is the smallest count on any router, and Rules counts all of them -- per router in the Routers table.",
   "id": 1,
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 5,
    "w": 5,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0
